From f20c1e21036557a7e4e9dd121b59fbb401e4fec5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Fable 5.1" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 07:15:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MP3PLAY: FILELEN never stalls the guest

A NatFeat handler runs inline on the emulated CPU, and for as long as it
takes the 68k is stalled. mpg123_scan() on a five-minute VBR file is a
second or more, and stalls that long inside a trap took the guest's timer
interrupts down: MP3GEM's clock stopped dead and only IKBD traffic from
moving the mouse nudged it forward. Twenty-two of them in a row at load
was worse.

So the NatFeat no longer reads anything. It returns -2 (pending) at once
and queues the path; a detached worker thread does the open/length/scan
with no lock held, and the answer is there the next time the guest asks.
A 64-slot cache means a folder is read once. Queued slots are never
evicted - the worker owns them - and if every slot is queued the caller
simply gets -2 again.

Whether a long inline stall SHOULD wedge the timer is a separate question
for the emulator; VIDPLAY.PLAY and STBOX.START stall too, once each, and
seem to get away with it. This patch just stops MP3PLAY doing it at all.

Applies on top of "MP3PLAY: FILELEN reads the header before it scans".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MGcLwq6U6E1QhD3W3PzuF7
